// The heap categories and fact kinds, declared once (R0-O12). This tree
// is part 2's (optimizer-ir.md Section 7) with the three categories
// JS-M0 adds under Heap: weak (gc_mutable: a cycle clears weak slots),
// kept and realm. T2's effect bitset and the operation facts are
// generated from this list. The Wasm categories arrive with W2.

category Heap;
category Field(key: i32) under Heap;        // named slots by key class; Field(any) is every key
category Elements(layout: i32) under Heap;  // indexed elements by layout
category FactHolder under Heap;             // slots and elements of objects with registered facts
category Context under Heap;                // scope slots
category Buffer(n: i32) under Heap;         // a buffer-table entry's backing store
category External(kind: i32) under Heap;    // node columns and external strings
category weak under Heap gc_mutable;        // weak slots: WeakRef targets, finalization cells
category kept under Heap;                   // the agent's [[KeptAlive]] list (outside the cage)
category realm under Heap;                  // the realm's random stream

// No fact kind exists at JS-M0: facts and their ledger arrive with T2
// (part 2, code-table-and-ledger.md). The declaration form is
//   fact NAME on FactHolder;
